// Bandit Level 19 → Level 20

URL: https://overthewire.org/wargames/bandit/

Step1: Log in to the Bandit Level 19 server:

        ssh bandit19@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step2: Enter the password obtained from Bandit Level 18.

Step3: List the files in the home directory:

        ls -la

Step4: We can see a special executable:

        bandit20-do

Step5: Run the binary without arguments to see how it works:

        ./bandit20-do

Step6: It shows that we can use it to run a command as another user:

        Run a command as another user.
        Example: ./bandit20-do id

Step7: Test which user the command runs as:

        ./bandit20-do whoami

Step8: The output is:

        bandit20

Step9: This means `bandit20-do` is a SUID binary owned by `bandit20`. 
       When we execute it, the command runs with bandit20's effective privileges.

Step10: The password for the next level is stored at:

        /etc/bandit_pass/bandit20

Step11: Use the SUID binary to read the password:

        ./bandit20-do cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit20

Step12: The password obtained is:

        0qXahG8ZjOVMN9Ghs7iOWsCfZyXOUbYO

Step13: The Bandit Level 19 → Level 20 challenge is solved.

